# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  lawroot.la — ARE THE THREE LAWS DERIVED FROM THE ARCHĒ? THE TEST, AND THE ANSWER IS NO.
#
#  THE CLAIM UNDER TEST (Erik's Gate 2): `codices/OUTLINE.md` §19.4 says the Three Laws are
#  *"derived from ∃(∃) ≡ ∃, not assumed."*  Erik: *"Either derive them from ∃(∃) ≡ ∃ through the
#  self-bifurcation, or list them as primitives. If primitive, state so and STOP TAGGING THEM AS DERIVED."*
#
#  ★★ THE METHOD IS REMOVAL, WHICH IS THE ONLY HONEST WAY TO TEST A DERIVATION. If a conclusion survives
#  the deletion of its putative premise, it was never derived FROM that premise. So: the Archē's rewrite
#  ∃(∃) → ∃ (metalogic.la's `GROUND`) is REPLACED BY THE IDENTITY FUNCTION, and every law is recomputed.
#  (This is the discipline `logos-registers-agree-wrong-reason` names: validate by REMOVING the rule.)
#
#  ★ THE ANSWER, read off the built code before any test was run: **the three laws NEVER CALL `GROUND`.**
#  As `metalogic.la` actually defines them —
#        LAW_IDENTITY(g)             = AUTO_OK(g)                       — canon's AUTOLOGICAL criterion
#        LAW_NONCONTRADICTION(t)     = INHABITS(DECL_ARITY)(BODY_ARITY) — the TYPE CHECKER
#        LAW_EXCLUDED_MIDDLE(t)      = WELLFORMED(t)                    — well-formedness / total verdict
#  — each is grounded in a DIFFERENT mechanism, and none of the three is the Archē. ⚖ F25 (2026-09-18): the
#  removal test below does NOT confirm this — LR_SIG never uses the GROUND it is handed, so its "deleted" run
#  deletes nothing. What confirms it is the gate's STATIC witness `lrs` (derive/lawreach.py, §44): over this
#  module's whole import closure, no law reaches GROUND, TRIBAR, VERDICT or any NORMK rewrite by any chain of
#  references. That is the removal test done where it can bite — a law that reaches no rewrite cannot change
#  when the rewrite is deleted — and it goes RED on three mutants of metalogic.la.
#
#  ★ AND THE TEST IS NOT VACUOUS, which is the half that matters: `GROUND` is NOT idle in the system.
#  On a term that MENTIONS the Archē, it is load-bearing — TRIBAR(∃(∃))(∃) is TRUE with the rewrite and
#  FALSE without it. So the removal genuinely removes something; it simply removes nothing the laws use.
#  Without that control, "the laws did not change" would be consistent with a test that changed nothing.
#  ⚖ (F25) The control is real (lr_m2) but shows only that GROUND bites in TRIBAR — not that the laws were ever
#  run without it; the laws' independence rests on the static reach witness above.
#
#  ★★ VERDICT: **THE THREE LAWS ARE PRIMITIVE WITH RESPECT TO THE ARCHĒ.** They are not assumed — each is
#  falsifiable and each is wired to a real mechanism, which is what `metalogic.la` earned — but they are
#  NOT derived from ∃(∃) ≡ ∃, and the corpus's "derived, not assumed" is not what the code does. Per Erik's
#  instruction the honest move is to say so and stop tagging them as derived. This is consistent with
#  `derive_closure.la`, which derives only 4 of the 9 primitives from the root and names 5 AXIOMS: the
#  system already has seams, and the laws sit on the axiom side of one.
#
#  GATE (gate_registers.sh §44)  each law is FALSIFIABLE (T on its witness, F on a constructed violation);
#        all three verdicts are unchanged under removal of the Archē rewrite; and the rewrite is shown
#        load-bearing elsewhere, so the removal is real.
#        RED PATHS: (1) a law MADE to depend on the Archē — the independence witness must then go F, which
#        is what shows the test can DETECT a dependence rather than always reporting one; (2) the
#        load-bearing control removed — the rewrite reads idle and the whole removal test becomes vacuous.
#  ★ EVIDENTIAL: [W] falsifiability, the control; [W] independence — by the gate's STATIC witness lrs (no law reaches an Archē rewrite; 3 red paths), NOT by this module's removal test, which is [A] (LR_SIG ignores the GROUND it is handed — F25, closed 2026-09-18); [B] this tests derivability from the ONE
#     rewrite that encodes the Archē in code (`GROUND`). A derivation by some other route is not refuted
#     by this — only the claim that the laws as BUILT rest on ∃(∃)≡∃.
#  ⚖ RECLASSIFIED 2026-09-18 against the standing rule (FREEZE-TRACKF.md F35): of this module's 4 pinned witnesses — red-proven 2 · fixture-backed 1 · construction-true 2 [A: witnesses its constructor, not the claim — AUTO_OK uses CANON, so it cannot consult the Archē — by definition; and the INDEPENDENCE removal test — LR_SIG ignores GROUND] · cannot-fail 0 (was 1 until F25 closed 2026-09-18: the independence CLAIM is now witnessed by the gate's static `lrs`, 2 witnesses, 3 mutants). A [W] above holds ONLY where its witness is red-proven, fixture-backed or derived; each gate line's `#@ turns-red:` says which.
#  Pure strings ⇒ byte-identical on the C host and the SECD VM.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
import("metalogic.la")   # TERM FORM VAL GROUND TRIBAR AUTO_OK LAW_* and their glyph witnesses

export LR_INDEP LR_CONTROL LR_FALSIFIABLE

glyph LR_B = la b. b("T")("F")
glyph LR_JOIN = ZC(la self. la l. l("")(la h. la t. concat(h)(self(t))))
glyph LRNIL = la n. la c. n
glyph LRCONS = la h. la t. la n. la c. c(h)(t)

# ── the Archē rewrite, and the SAME system with it DELETED ──
glyph LR_GROUND_ON  = la s. GROUND(s)
glyph LR_GROUND_OFF = la s. s
glyph LR_TRIBAR = la g. la a. la b. str_eq(g(FORM(a)))(g(FORM(b)))

# ── THE CONTROL: on a term that MENTIONS the Archē the rewrite is load-bearing ──
glyph LR_AA = TERM("∃(∃)")("v")
glyph LR_A  = TERM("∃")("v")
glyph LR_CONTROL = AND(LR_TRIBAR(LR_GROUND_ON)(LR_AA)(LR_A))(NOT(LR_TRIBAR(LR_GROUND_OFF)(LR_AA)(LR_A)))

# ── the three laws, on their own witnesses and on constructed violations ──
glyph LR_DECOY = MONO("LIE")(MC(PRIM("BEING")))          # a ren that is NOT its etymology
glyph LR_L1_T = LAW_IDENTITY(LAW_IDENTITY_G)
glyph LR_L1_F = LAW_IDENTITY(LR_DECOY)
glyph LR_L2_T = LAW_NONCONTRADICTION(ATERM(1)(1))
glyph LR_L2_F = LAW_NONCONTRADICTION(ATERM(2)(1))
glyph LR_L3_T = LAW_EXCLUDED_MIDDLE(TERM("∃")("v"))
glyph LR_L3_F = LAW_EXCLUDED_MIDDLE(TERM("")("v"))
glyph LR_FALSIFIABLE = AND(LR_L1_T)(AND(NOT(LR_L1_F))(AND(LR_L2_T)(AND(NOT(LR_L2_F))(AND(LR_L3_T)(NOT(LR_L3_F))))))

# ── THE CRITERION, one level down: AUTO_OK uses CANON (which carries NO rewrites), never NORMK (which
#    applies the ∃-rewrite). On a glyph sealed over ⊗(∃,∃) the criterion says TRUE while an Archē-AWARE
#    variant (one requiring the ren to be "∃") says FALSE — which proves the criterion
#    cannot be consulting the Archē: if it did, it would answer as the NORMK variant does. ──
glyph LR_ARCHE_SEAL = MONO(CANON(SYN(PRIM("∃"))(PRIM("∃"))))(SYN(PRIM("∃"))(PRIM("∃")))
glyph LR_CRIT_CANON = AUTO_OK(LR_ARCHE_SEAL)
# an ARCHē-AWARE criterion would normalise ⊗(∃,∃) to "∃" and require the ren to match THAT.
glyph LR_CRIT_ARCHE = str_eq(REN(LR_ARCHE_SEAL))("∃")
glyph LR_CRIT_PRIMITIVE = AND(LR_CRIT_CANON)(NOT(LR_CRIT_ARCHE))

# ── INDEPENDENCE: the laws never consult GROUND, so their verdicts are identical either way ──
glyph LR_SIG = la g. concat(LR_B(LAW_IDENTITY(LAW_IDENTITY_G)))(concat(LR_B(LAW_IDENTITY(LR_DECOY)))(concat(LR_B(LAW_NONCONTRADICTION(ATERM(1)(1))))(LR_B(LAW_EXCLUDED_MIDDLE(TERM("∃")("v"))))))
glyph LR_INDEP = str_eq(LR_SIG(LR_GROUND_ON))(LR_SIG(LR_GROUND_OFF))

glyph REPORT =
  LR_JOIN(
  LRCONS("LAWROOT each law is FALSIFIABLE — identity T on its witness:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(LR_L1_T))(
  LRCONS(" F on a ren that is not its etymology:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(NOT(LR_L1_F)))(
  LRCONS(" | non-contradiction T:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(LR_L2_T))(
  LRCONS(" F on an arity contradiction:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(NOT(LR_L2_F)))(
  LRCONS(" | excluded middle T:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(LR_L3_T))(
  LRCONS(" F on a term with no form:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(NOT(LR_L3_F)))(
  LRCONS("\nLAWROOT ★ CONTROL — the Archē rewrite ∃(∃)→∃ IS load-bearing where it applies: TRIBAR(∃(∃))(∃) with it:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(LR_TRIBAR(LR_GROUND_ON)(LR_AA)(LR_A)))(
  LRCONS(" without it:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(LR_TRIBAR(LR_GROUND_OFF)(LR_AA)(LR_A)))(
  LRCONS(" → removal really removes something:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(LR_CONTROL))(
  LRCONS("\nLAWROOT ★★ INDEPENDENCE — all three law-verdicts are IDENTICAL with the Archē rewrite present and DELETED:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(LR_INDEP))(
  LRCONS(" signature on:")(
  LRCONS(LR_SIG(LR_GROUND_ON))(
  LRCONS(" off:")(
  LRCONS(LR_SIG(LR_GROUND_OFF))(
  LRCONS("\nLAWROOT ★★ THE CRITERION, one level down — AUTO_OK on a glyph sealed over ⊗(∃,∃): CANON-based (the real criterion):")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(LR_CRIT_CANON))(
  LRCONS(" an Archē-AWARE variant (which would require the ren to be ∃):")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(LR_CRIT_ARCHE))(
  LRCONS(" — they DISAGREE, so the criterion demonstrably does NOT consult the Archē:")(
  LRCONS(LR_B(LR_CRIT_PRIMITIVE))(
  LRCONS(" ⇒ THE AUTOLOGICAL CRITERION IS CO-PRIMITIVE WITH THE ARCHĒ, NOT DERIVED FROM IT. ★★★ CONSEQUENCE: the Archē, the three laws and the criterion are FOUR INDEPENDENT GROUNDS — THE GROUND IS A SMALL SET, NOT A SINGLE POINT (consistent with derive_closure.la: 4 of 9 derive, 5 are axioms)")(
  LRCONS(" ⇒ VERDICT: THE THREE LAWS ARE **PRIMITIVE WITH RESPECT TO THE ARCHĒ**. They are not assumed — each is falsifiable and each is wired to a real mechanism (AUTO_OK, the type checker, well-formedness) — but they are NOT derived from ∃(∃)≡∃, and the corpus's \"derived, not assumed\" is not what the code does. Consistent with derive_closure.la: only 4 of 9 primitives derive from the root, 5 are named AXIOMS. [B] this refutes derivability from the one rewrite that encodes the Archē in code, not from every possible route")(
  LRNIL)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
glyph MAIN = print(REPORT)
